
The first version of the Working Day Planner module is ready for testing.
It is a yearly work-day / holiday planning tool: the user marks days on the
calendar (work / half day / off), can add a note, and sees the net working
days count live.

How to open:
- Open the file directly in a browser, OR
- In the folder: python -m http.server 8000 -> http://localhost:8000

Test scenarios:
1. Click a day -> a popover opens; select Work / Half day / Off, enter a note,
   and Save. (It should also close with Esc / clicking outside.)
2. Do the net working days counter and monthly totals update instantly?
   (half day = 0.5)
3. Weekends (Sat-Sun) are off by default; a holiday marked on a weekday should
   appear in red.
4. Do days with a note show a corner dot + hover tooltip?
5. Year selector (< 2026 >) - does the calendar rebuild when the year changes?
6. Download CSV -> are all days, statuses and notes in the file?
   (Excel-TR: ";" separated, UTF-8 BOM)
7. Responsive: does the column count drop 4 -> 3 -> 2 -> 1 as the window narrows?

Known limitations (do not report as bugs):
- No persistence - marks are lost on page refresh (intentional).
- Weekend policy is fixed to Sat+Sun (the selector UI was removed).
- Official holidays are not auto-filled.

Environment: latest Chrome/Edge/Firefox. Please report any bugs with a
screenshot + steps to reproduce.

