OTHER CHANGES IN THIS BUILD (besides the Working Day planner page)

The same commit also touched a few other areas - please regression-test
these as well:

1. Workload list - filters reworked
   - Removed the Task Type, Status, Complexity and free-text Search filters.
   - Added a Team filter and a Category filter.
   - The Project dropdown is now disabled (and cleared) when the selected
     Activity Type is not "Project".
   - The Category filter resets automatically when the Activity Type changes
     (categories are scoped to the activity type).
   Test: apply/clear each filter, switch activity types, confirm the
   project/category dropdowns enable/reset correctly and the active-filter
   count is right.

2. Team filter on backend endpoints
   - Workload list, export and aggregates endpoints now accept a team_id
     filter (scopes results to the accounts on that team).
   Test: filtering by team returns only that team's entries in the table,
   the CSV export and the KPI/aggregate numbers.

3. Permissions - working-days editing restricted (new requirement)
   - Manager and Tech Lead can no longer edit working days (report is now
     read-only for them). Only Admin and QA Specialist can edit.
     Note: this is an intentional new requirement, not a bug.
   Test: log in as Manager/Tech Lead -> no edit access to working days;
   as Admin/QA -> editing works.

4. Yearly report - old inline working-days editor removed
   - The "Edit/View days" button and its popup editor were removed from the
     Yearly Report screen (editing now lives in the new planner page).
   Test: yearly report still loads, colors and Excel export work; the old
   edit button is gone.

5. My Workload calendar - holiday/leave awareness
   - Calendar cells now reflect planner marks: holidays/leave shown in a
     distinct color, half-days use a half-day target, notes appear on the
     cell with a tooltip.
   Test: mark a holiday/half-day/leave in the planner, then check the
   My Workload calendar reflects the color, note and target.

6. Workload entry - holiday confirmation
   - Logging a new entry on a day marked as a holiday/leave (or a weekend)
     now shows a confirmation dialog first.
   Test: try to log work on a marked holiday/weekend -> confirm dialog
   appears; confirming saves, cancelling does not.

7. Half-day support in working-days data model
   - Expected working days now allow fractional values (e.g. 21.5) so
     half-days flow into monthly net totals and the yearly report target.
   Test: a month containing half-days shows a fractional net/target
   without rounding errors.
